Every crafted file is handled:
- the 16,384-column file takes 0.16 s, down from 34 s;
- the 100 MB-cell zip bomb is rejected in 0.5 s;
- a legitimate 300k-row file still reads, in 5 s.

Committing:

I've opened issue #18 with all the security findings, and fixed findings 1–4 on PR #17. All checks pass, and the real-data output is still byte-identical after every commit.

**Issue #18: 安全：处理不可信输入（提示注入优先）与 #17 审计发现**
- **Prompt injection comes first.** Player text will reach the LLM in #6, and the planned agent loop will let the model choose its own tool calls based on that text, which makes injection more dangerous. The issue lists the measures to build into #6 and #12:
  - mark the email body as data in prompts, and strip or flag invisible and direction-changing characters;
  - injected content must never trigger auto-send;
  - tools read-only and limited to the current case;
  - output checks on drafts;
  - injection samples in the #7 evaluation set.
- **It also tracks the rest:**
  - players faking agent or system roles (which can also poison the template base);
  - the two smaller slowdowns;
  - downstream handling (UI escaping, CSV export, allowed characters in `Case.id`);
  - the list of things the audit checked and found fine.
- **It's a tracking issue, not a one-time design.** Every feature PR that handles untrusted input checks against it and updates it, and it gets written up as `docs/security.md` once there's enough to say. I left a comment there saying which items #17 fixes.

**Fixes on #17** (5 signed commits, pushed):

| Finding | Fix | Measured |
|---|---|---|
| 1. Slow regexes | Rewrote the header, separator and trailing-space patterns to run in linear time; added a test file of crafted inputs | 30k-character input: 2–5 s → under 5 ms |
| 2. Crafted spreadsheets exhaust resources | Read only 3 columns; cap uncompressed size at 200 MB, rows at 1,048,576, bodies at 32,767 characters, IDs at 64 characters; added `defusedxml` (its own commit) | 16,384-column file: 34 s → 0.16 s; zip bomb rejected in 0.5 s |
| 3. Raw crash on a bad cell | Message numbers must be ≥1 and at most 18 digits; any read failure is reported as one format error | No crafted file produces a raw exception |
| 4. Errors echo cell content | Long values show only their length; short values and thread IDs are escaped | Longest error message is 61 characters, all printable |

The PR description now has a "安全加固（#18）" section and references #18. I haven't checked whether CodeRabbit has commented on these new commits; tell me when you'd like me to look.

